{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only two completed experiments. config_002 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) achieved 52.0% accuracy, while config_041 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) achieved only 22.7%, indicating RNA is the dominant modality and image is very weak in this setup. Uncertainty: It is unknown whether the scvi_n200 learned latent representation is actually superior to a simpler linear projection (PCA) for this task. Question tested: config_010 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) differs from config_002 in exactly one variable—the RNA encoder—so it cleanly isolates the effect of learned vs. linear representation while holding model setting, profile setting, and all other hyperparameters constant. Why this is the best next experiment: With a limited budget and only two data points, establishing whether the more complex scvi encoder provides a real advantage over PCA is a foundational question. If PCA matches or exceeds scvi, it simplifies the design space and suggests the bottleneck is elsewhere (e.g., profile setting or fusion). If scvi is clearly better, it validates investing in learned representations for subsequent multimodal experiments. Either outcome sharply reduces uncertainty before committing experiments to multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

